1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:14,120
Welcome to Tejasvi. In this tutorial we will set up a school from the very beginning: signing in, entering the school, its teachers, classes and students, then the daily routine, examinations, fees, and reports.

2
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:28,869
Tejasvi has three parts. EMIS is the school office. Tejasvi Learning is where teaching happens online. The Tejasvi app brings both to the phone. A student is entered once, in EMIS, and every part uses the same record.

3
00:00:30,069 --> 00:00:43,460
Open your Tejasvi address and choose Log in. Enter the email and temporary password you were given. You will be asked to choose a new password of at least twelve characters. Then open My workspaces, choose your school, and open EMIS.

4
00:00:44,660 --> 00:01:04,854
Go to Settings, then Institution profile. Enter the official name, school code, address, phone, PAN and the principal’s name. Check the academic year. Set the attendance threshold, absence SMS and the library fine per day, then save. These details are printed on grade sheets, certificates and ID cards.

5
00:01:06,054 --> 00:01:26,274
Next, add a department, then your teachers under Staff and access, Faculty. You can add them one by one or import a spreadsheet. To give someone a login, open Users and access, choose Add account, pick their role, and share the temporary password privately. A teacher’s login is linked to their record, so they see only their own classes.

6
00:01:27,474 --> 00:01:45,627
Now create your classes. Each section is its own record, such as Grade 6 A and Grade 6 B, with a class teacher. Then add the subjects for each section with their credit hours, theory and internal full marks, and the subject teacher. Subjects marked Additional appear on the grade sheet but are not counted in GPA.

7
00:01:46,827 --> 00:02:04,927
To load existing students, open the Student directory and choose Import. Download the template, fill one row per student, and write the class the way it is named, for example Grade 6 A. Choose the file, click Validate and review, fix any row it names, and save. Nothing is saved until every row passes.

8
00:02:06,127 --> 00:02:22,566
To give a parent access, open the student’s record and choose Parent access. Enter the parent’s name and email and a temporary password. Parents then see only their own children: attendance, homework, published results, fees and notices. They can also send leave notes.

9
00:02:23,766 --> 00:02:32,471
Each morning the school home page shows which classes have not taken attendance, the fees outstanding, leave notes waiting for review, and the latest notices.

10
00:02:33,671 --> 00:02:48,289
The class teacher opens Take attendance and chooses the class. Everyone starts as present, so you only tap A for absent, L for late, or Lv for leave, then save. If absence SMS is switched on, parents of absent children get a message.

11
00:02:49,489 --> 00:03:01,432
Add homework or classwork for a class and subject with a due date. After the due date, open Check homework, mark who did part or none, and save. Students and parents see open homework on their home page.

12
00:03:02,632 --> 00:03:19,387
For examinations, first create the examination, such as First Terminal. Teachers then open Enter marks, choose the class and subject, and type theory and internal marks. The letter grade appears as they type. Teachers save drafts; the examination coordinator publishes.

13
00:03:20,587 --> 00:03:34,341
Grade sheets show the whole class ledger with grades, GPA, rank and attendance. A subject is not graded below thirty-five percent in theory or forty percent internal. When everything is checked, print all grade sheets, one per page.

14
00:03:35,541 --> 00:03:52,877
Set the fee structure once: tuition per class, transport for bus users, lunch, and exam fees. Each month, open Monthly billing, choose the month and classes, preview every bill with scholarships already deducted, and create the invoices. Students already billed are skipped.

15
00:03:54,077 --> 00:04:00,970
Add bus routes with their stops and vehicle, and choose the route on each bus student’s record. For every trip, mark who boarded.

16
00:04:02,170 --> 00:04:10,443
At the library desk, scan or type the book’s accession number and the student’s ID to issue a book. Returns calculate the late fine automatically.

17
00:04:11,643 --> 00:04:22,346
Print ID cards for a whole class at card size, with a QR code of the student ID. Character, transfer and bonafide certificates are issued with their own numbers and printed on the school letterhead.

18
00:04:23,546 --> 00:04:34,021
Set each person’s salary structure, including SSF, CIT and tax. Each month, preview payroll and create payslips for everyone in one step, then print them.

19
00:04:35,221 --> 00:04:47,714
For government reporting, the IEMIS page counts students by class, sex, caste and disability, and teachers by sex. Download the figures as a spreadsheet and copy them into the official Flash form.

20
00:04:48,914 --> 00:05:04,794
In Tejasvi Learning, students from EMIS appear in the student directory, where you give each one a login. Create a batch for each section, assign subjects and teachers, then teachers publish lessons, quizzes and assignments. Students can learn on the app, even offline.

21
00:05:05,994 --> 00:05:22,022
At the end of the year, publish the final results and mark students who left. Then open Promote students, tick any students who repeat their class, preview, and promote. Next year’s classes, subjects and fees are created, and last year’s records stay exactly as they were.

22
00:05:23,222 --> 00:05:33,228
That is the whole year in Tejasvi. Keep the Tejasvi School Handbook beside you: it has every step, the import templates and a checklist for your first month. Thank you for watching.
